   "slot": "member1_opening",
   "text": "A price crash for LUSD triggers the Stability Pool and debt redistribution, not forced sales. Before the shock, collateral coverage sits at 3.33; after the shock it rises to 3.38 as the mechanism restores balance. The system records no bad debt because no trove reaches the minimum collateral ratio on the ruled grid, and the first liquidation would require an ETH shock of -30.26%.\n\nThe exit liquidity available in this scenario is $10.2M, yet forced sales equal zero since absorption offsets debt against the pool rather than selling collateral. Liquidity providers leave with a share of zero, leaving the full Stability Pool balance to absorb the impact.\n\nThis outcome holds across all shock levels shown: even when exit liquidity drops to $6.8M in later scenarios, the ratio of forced sales to exit liquidity remains zero because no forced sale exists on the absorption path.",
