   "text": "A depeg of the paired stablecoin fits this token's mechanism because it is structurally insulated by construction, meaning exposure occurs only through exit venues rather than forced sales. The recomputed exit-liquidity curves show that when the paired stablecoin trades at its middle target of 0.93, the available depth is $9.5M at a price impact of 1.0%. At lower targets like 0.88, liquidity drops to $7.7M at the same impact level, while higher targets such as 0.97 provide $9.3M under identical conditions.\n\nThe stability-module contribution remains zero across all these scenarios, confirming that no forced sales occur in the Member-2 headline depeg scenario. Instead, the system relies entirely on the existing pool depth to absorb shocks without triggering liquidations. This design ensures that the token's value adjusts through market mechanics rather than internal sell-offs.",
