      "text": "The counterfactual where the price feed falls back from Chainlink to the Tellor oracle affects the measure that relies on that specific data source. This change alters how the system observes prices when the primary feed is unavailable, shifting reliance to an alternative network.\n\nBecause LUSD carries no lagged moving-average price line and lacks a per-market price EMA, the fallback does not introduce smoothing delays found in other protocols. The price basis remains the bundle's own total collateral value divided by the total collateral amount, which is read instantly at the report's block rather than from a re-simulated fresh price-feed read.\n\nThe last good price is disclosed beside the current reading and lags by design, as only a fresh price-feed read rewrites it. This structural behavior means the fallback to Tellor operates within the existing lag framework without creating new latency."
